/test_native_test_verification.py-1136-\n\n[Showing lines 42-534 of 534 (50.0KB limit). Full output: /tmp/pi-bash-f6cf8b97653e5016.log]"}], "details": {"truncation": {"content": "docs/DEVELOPING.md:318:- Merge native trace metadata: `./gradlew mergeNativeTraceMetadata -PinputDirs=<absolute-trace-output-dir-0>,<absolute-trace-output-dir-1>,... -PoutputDir=<absolute-merged-metadata-dir>`\ndocs/DEVELOPING.md:319:- Split test-only metadata: `./gradlew splitTestOnlyMetadata -Pcoordinates=[group:artifact:version|group:artifact|k/n|all]`\ndocs/DEVELOPING.md-320-- Fix test that fails Native Image run for new library version: `./gradlew fixTestNativeImageRun -PtestLibraryCoordinates=group:artifact:version -PnewLibraryVersion=version`\ndocs/DEVELOPING.md-321-- Test (single lib): `./gradlew test -Pcoordinates=[group:artifact:version|k/n|all]`\ndocs/DEVELOPING.md-322-- List resolved tested-library jars: `./gradlew listLibraryJars -Pcoordinates=[group:artifact:version|k/n|all]`\n--\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-164-| Task | Purpose |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-165-| --- | --- |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-166-| `nativeTraceImage` | Build a native image instrumented with the tracing agent. |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md:167:| `runNativeTraceImage` | Run it to collect access traces. |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md:168:| `mergeNativeTraceMetadata` | Merge collected traces into metadata. |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-169-| `generateDynamicAccessReport` | Report the dynamic access a coordinate exercises. |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-170-\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-171-## 5. Metadata authoring helpers\n--\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-177-| `scaffold` | Create the test project and metadata skeleton for a new coordinate from the scaffold templates (§AR-build-infrastructure). |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-178-| `contribute` | Guided contribution flow for a new coordinate. |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-179-| `generateMetadata` | Generate metadata for a coordinate (optionally deriving `user-code-filter.json` from the resolved JAR). |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md:180:| `splitTestOnlyMetadata` | Move test-only metadata into test resources (§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.1, §FS-metadata). |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-181-| `routeForeignMetadata` | After metadata validation fails, relocate uniquely owned foreign-condition entries to supported artifact/version buckets, validate the affected owners, and regenerate their statistics (§FS-metadata). |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-182-| `fixTestNativeImageRun` | Regenerate metadata for a new version failing a native-image run. |\ndocs/architecture/tck.md-183-| `addTestedVersion` | Record a newly passing version in the artifact's `index.json` and refresh the mirrored stats and shared test sources; used by the compatibility workflow (§FS-repository-functional-spec.9). |\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-58-- Compilation, JVM-mode tests (`javaTest`), and native-image tests (`nativeTest`).\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-59-- Coverage collection (JaCoCo) and dynamic-access reporting per coordinate.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-60-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:61:The harness uses a single coordinates filter `-Pcoordinates=` accepting `all`, `group:artifact`, `group:artifact:version`, or shard `k/n`. It also exposes authoring helpers (`generateMetadata`, `splitTestOnlyMetadata`, `fixTestNativeImageRun`, `addTestedVersion`, `fetchExistingLibrariesWithNewerVersions`), reporting tasks (`jacocoTestReport`, `generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport`, `generateLibraryStats`, `analyzeExternalLibraryDynamicAccess`, `listTopCoordinatesByMetric`, `generateTopCoordinatesByMetricMatrix`), and the `package` release task. Its task groups and the Gradle harness that delegates `-Pcoordinates=` to per-coordinate sub-builds are specified in §AR-test-harness; the test sources it drives in §FS-tests. The full task reference lives in [DEVELOPING.md](../DEVELOPING.md).\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-62-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-63-### 4.3 Continuous integration\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-64-§AR-repository-ci\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-222-- **No test-only shipped entries.** A metadata entry is test-only when the type it describes belongs to a package from the test suite; such entries must not ship. A type from the library JAR or one of its dependencies is library metadata even when a test is what exercised it.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-223-- **Index coverage.** Each `metadata/<group>/<artifact>/` directory must include a valid `index.json` enumerating its metadata versions and tested library versions.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-224-- **Single latest entry.** Exactly one entry in a non-empty `index.json` must carry `latest: true`. If a library version is not in `tested-versions`, the harness selects an entry by matching the optional `default-for` regex.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:225:- **Dependency and test-only split.** Metadata can declare dependencies on other artifacts via `requires`. Metadata needed only by the tests — entries whose type or `typeReached` names a test package, or whose resource is a test resource — must not ship to consumers; `splitTestOnlyMetadata` moves them out of the library's `reachability-metadata.json` into the test project's `src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json`, keeping the shipped metadata free of test-only types (§FS-metadata).\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-226-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-227-### 5.2 Tests\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-228-\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md-17-  harness runs on the JVM and on `native-image`.\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md-18-- `src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json`\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md-19-  — when present, the test-only reachability metadata that\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md:20:  `splitTestOnlyMetadata` carved out of the shipped library metadata so the test\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md-21-  image can reach its own helper types without those entries reaching consumers\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md-22-  (§FS-metadata, §FS-repository-functional-spec.5.1).\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md-23-- `build.gradle` may add test dependencies and, when there is no better public\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-79-Tests routinely need reachability metadata for their *own* helper types — the\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-80-test classes, fixtures, and resources that exercise the library — but those\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-81-entries must never reach a consumer (§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.1). The\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:82:harness `splitTestOnlyMetadata` task (§AR-test-harness.5) maintains that\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-83-separation: any entry whose `type` or `condition.typeReached` names a test\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-84-package, or whose resource is a test resource, is moved out of the library's\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-85-`metadata/<group>/<artifact>/<version>/reachability-metadata.json` and into the\n--\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org.graalvm.internal.tck.gradle-239-\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org.graalvm.internal.tck.gradle-240-boolean informationalTaskRequested = isTaskRequested(\"help\") || isTaskRequested(\"tasks\") || isTaskRequested(\"properties\")\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org.graalvm.internal.tck.gradle-241-boolean nativeTraceImageTaskRequested = !informationalTaskRequested &&\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org.graalvm.internal.tck.gradle:242:        (isTaskRequested(\"nativeTraceImage\") || isTaskRequested(\"runNativeTraceImage\"))\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org.graalvm.internal.tck.gradle:243:boolean runNativeTraceImageTaskRequested = !informationalTaskRequested && isTaskRequested(\"runNativeTraceImage\")\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org.graalvm.intern